{"type":"npc","name":"Spectral Conductor","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":100,"temp":0,"max":100,"details":"void healing"},"ac":{"value":26,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":0,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":25}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"death-effects","exceptions":[]},{"type":"paralyzed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]},{"type":"precision","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"all-damage","value":8,"exceptions":["force","ghost-touch","spirit","vitality"],"doubleVs":["non-magical"]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","melodian","necril"],"details":""},"level":{"value":8},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Even in death, a spectral conductor desires simply to conduct performances in front of an audience, creating music to delight their audience from beyond the grave. On their own, spectral conductors are relatively harmless compared to other creatures with a similar amount of power. At worst, they might try to recruit passing travelers for their band or hold a concert or practice at an inopportune time and place, such as the middle of the night inside an unsuspecting person's bedchamber. While this can be inconvenient, when considering what else they might be capable of doing, these acts might seems like mere pranks or shenanigans in comparison.</p><p>Spectral conductors recruit anyone they can find who is willing to sing or play an instrument—even those who most people might consider to be talentless hacks... or even bloodthirsty monsters. As a result, their concerts are prone to becoming gatherings of dangerous creatures that could easily wreak havoc in the local area after the performance is over. It's easy to see how this can put authority figures and security personnel on edge, potentially causing them to engage in a preemptive attack against the perceived threat. However, this aggressive action can increase the danger, since attacking any member of the spectral conductor's band during a rehearsal or performance is sure to inspire the otherwise-peaceful spectral conductor to join the fray on behalf of their concertmates. This can quickly turn what was a peaceful, if bizarre, concert into a devastating life or death battle.</p><h2>Battle of the Bands</h2><p>Spectral conductors welcome all who wish to perform regardless of talent, finding beauty in any earnest expression. Their ethos puts them at odds with storm conductors, who brutally punish those who fail to measure up to their standards. Spectral conductors often attempt to upstage storm conductors by building more popular bands, and they are quick to lash out at their more cantankerous counterparts with a blast of discordant noise should they attempt to interfere with a performance.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 64/140/250 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Deception, Diplomacy, Lore [Music], Performance, Society)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> charisma, death, dexterity, energy resistant (acid, cold, electricity, fire, void), fortification, intelligence, music, sensory (darkvision), time, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Joseph Cassidy","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":-5},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":3},"int":{"mod":4},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":6}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":19,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":13,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":16,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":19,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":16},"deception":{"base":16},"diplomac